<title>HONG KONG: Thai Airways jet hits turbulence, five injured.</title>
<headline>Thai Airways jet hits turbulence, five injured.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five passengers aboard a Thai Airways International Airbus were injured when the airliner hit turbulence on a flight from Bangkok to Hong Kong, a government spokesman said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The five, four women and a man, were taken to hospital after the plane carrying more than 300 passengers landed safely at Hong Kong's Kai Tak Airport on Friday night, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Two of the injured were still in hospital on Saturday, he said. No further details were available.</p>
